I found the relevant code. Here's the analysis:

## Current behaviour

In `pkg/cmd/gist/create/create.go`, the function `createRun` (lines 104–175) builds two messages: `processMessage` ("Creating gist...") and `completionMessage` ("Created gist"), which are printed to stderr.

The privacy status (`public`/`secret`, colored via `cs.Red("public")` / `cs.Green("secret")`) is only baked into `completionMessage` inside the `if gistName != "" {...}` block (lines 120–131):

```go
gistName := guessGistName(files)

processMessage := "Creating gist..."
completionMessage := "Created gist"
if gistName != "" {
    if len(files) > 1 {
        processMessage = "Creating gist with multiple files"
    } else {
        processMessage = fmt.Sprintf("Creating gist %s", gistName)
    }
    if opts.Public {
        completionMessage = fmt.Sprintf("Created %s gist %s", cs.Red("public"), gistName)
    } else {
        completionMessage = fmt.Sprintf("Created %s gist %s", cs.Green("secret"), gistName)
    }
}
```

`gistName` comes from `guessGistName(files)` (lines 229–246), which returns `""` unless there's at least one file whose name doesn't match the auto-generated `gistfileN.txt` pattern — i.e., it's empty when reading from stdin without `--filename`/`-f`, or when all filenames are stdin-style. In that case, `completionMessage` stays the generic `"Created gist"` string, with no mention of `public`/`secret` at all. So today, the privacy status only appears in the success message when a real filename is known.

## What needs to change

- **`pkg/cmd/gist/create/create.go`** — specifically `createRun`: the privacy-status logic (currently nested inside `if gistName != ""`) needs to be pulled out so `completionMessage` always includes the `public`/`secret` label, regardless of whether `gistName` is empty. E.g. something like always computing `completionMessage = fmt.Sprintf("Created %s gist %s", <color>, gistName)` (with `gistName` possibly being blank/omitted) while keeping the `gistName != ""` branch only for the filename-specific parts of `processMessage`/`completionMessage`.

Likely `pkg/cmd/gist/create/create_test.go` would also need updating to assert the new unconditional output (existing tests probably assert the plain `"Created gist"` string for the no-filename/stdin case).

No other files are involved — the privacy flag (`opts.Public`) and gist creation (`createGist`) are unaffected; this is purely an output-formatting change in `createRun`.
